{"kind":"assert","text":"The race gate is red on unmodified main. At main 5ff5d4db, go test -race -count=1 ./internal/kernel/ fails: TestCheckpointCacheScratchPreflightRefusesBeforeAllocation at checkpoint_cache_test.go:824 reports \"preflight refusal allocated 9 times; the names slice must not be allocated for scratch the budget refuses\". The same test passes without -race at the same tree, and fails identically under -race on an unrelated dependency-update branch, so this is an allocation-count assertion meeting race-detector instrumentation (which itself allocates), not a behaviour change. Every other package passes -race. Discovered while running the race gate for the dependency-update head 839dfe66; that lane reports it and proceeds, since the failure is present with and without the change. The repair is to make the allocation assertion race-aware — guard it so the alloc-count claim is only enforced when the race detector is off, keeping the functional refusal-before-allocation behaviour tested under both."}